From: nuubOS <nuubos@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] egl/wayland: wait for the frame callback after the commit
 (NUUBOS_SWAP_WAIT_AFTER)

eglSwapBuffers waits for the frame callback of the swap before, then
attaches and commits the new frame. A client that renders right after
the callback (RetroArch with vsync) then commits every frame just after
the compositor has composed: on the H700 with labwc, RetroArch's swap
returned 0.5 ms after each vblank, labwc composed at 0.27 ms, so each
frame waited ~15 ms in the swap, then a refresh in labwc, then the
scan-out: three refreshes from the core's input poll to the screen.
NUUBOS_SWAP_WAIT_AFTER=1 makes the swap commit at once and wait for that
frame's callback before returning: same frame rate, one refresh less.
Without the variable nothing changes.

Signed-off-by: nuubOS
---
--- a/src/egl/drivers/dri2/platform_wayland.c
+++ b/src/egl/drivers/dri2/platform_wayland.c
@@ -1480,6 +1480,19 @@
    .getCapability = dri2_wl_get_capability,
 };
 
+/* nuubOS: NUUBOS_SWAP_WAIT_AFTER=1, see dri2_wl_swap_buffers_with_damage. */
+static bool
+nuubos_swap_wait_after(void)
+{
+   static int on = -1;
+
+   if (on < 0) {
+      const char *v = getenv("NUUBOS_SWAP_WAIT_AFTER");
+      on = v && v[0] == '1';
+   }
+   return on;
+}
+
 static void
 wayland_throttle_callback(void *data, struct wl_callback *callback,
                           uint32_t time)
@@ -1762,6 +1775,18 @@
 
    wl_display_flush(dri2_dpy->wl_dpy);
 
+   /* nuubOS: wait for this frame's callback now, after its commit, instead
+    * of at the start of the next swap before that frame's commit. With the
+    * wait first, a client that renders right after the callback commits
+    * each frame just after the compositor has composed, so every frame
+    * waits a whole refresh in the swap before it is even attached. Same
+    * frame rate, one refresh less from input to screen. */
+   if (draw->SwapInterval > 0 && nuubos_swap_wait_after())
+      while (dri2_surf->throttle_callback != NULL)
+         if (loader_wayland_dispatch(dri2_dpy->wl_dpy, dri2_surf->wl_queue,
+                                     NULL) == -1)
+            return -1;
+
    return EGL_TRUE;
 }
 
